  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Monday)\nIssued at 952 PM CDT Mon Aug 17 2026\n\nTowards the end of the work week, we will be monitoring a series\nof shortwaves set to push southeast into the Tennessee Valley. As\na result, low to medium chances of rainfall return Thursday into\nFriday. A frontal boundary should shift southward through the area\nby Friday night, bringing dry conditions behind it through the\nweekend. Highs will be consistent through the long term period,\nwith highs in the upper 80s to mid 90s accompanied by heat indices\nin the upper 90s to around 104 degrees. While no heat products are\non the table at this time, we continue to encourage everyone to\nremain hydrated and practice heat safety to avoid heat related\nillness.",
